You can use the map function to create a new array, and then use the ... object spread syntax to create a copy of the changed object for the new array:

    import { useState } from 'react';

    const initialProducts = [{
      id: 0,
      name: 'Baklava',
      count: 1,
    }, {
      id: 1,
      name: 'Cheese',
